  "body": "## beads v1.3.3\n\nPre-compiled binaries for Linux, macOS (Intel & Apple Silicon), Windows (AMD64 & ARM64), Android/Termux (ARM64), and FreeBSD.\n\n### Release notes\n\nRead the full notes in [CHANGELOG.md](https://github.com/gastownhall/beads/blob/v1.3.3/CHANGELOG.md): the `[1.3.3]` and `[1.3.3-rc.1]` sections. They cover the security fixes, data-loss fixes and dependency updates, the **Upgrade notes** on what commands now accept or print, and the **Known issues** with their workarounds.\n\n### Known issue found after release: `GT_ROOT` in `.beads/.env` is ignored\n\n1.3.3 imports only an allowlist of keys from a project's `.beads/.env` (#7879). Gas City's `gc rig add` writes `GT_ROOT=<city root>` into each rig's `.beads/.env`, and 1.3.3 drops it. Every bd command in a rig prints `beads: ignoring GT_ROOT from .beads/.env` on stderr.\n\n- **Gas City: failed bd commands in a rig can be misreported.** gc exports `GT_ROOT` into agent sessions itself, so formulas still resolve. But released gc versions read bd's JSON error from stdout only when stderr is empty, and the notice fills stderr. A bd failure in a rig (for example a missing id) can therefore surface as the notice text instead of bd's error. gc's fix is gastownhall/gascity#8817.\n- **When you run `bd` by hand in a rig without `GT_ROOT` exported,** the city's formulas (`$GT_ROOT/.beads/formulas`) and town molecules are not found. The repo's own `.beads/formulas` and `~/.beads/formulas` still work. Workaround: `export GT_ROOT=<path to your city>` before running bd in a rig.\n\nNothing else is affected: no data, Dolt server selection or credentials. **bd 1.3.4** will allow `GT_ROOT` from `.beads/.env` again (#8117), which removes the notice for every gc version.\n\n### Installation\n\n**Homebrew (macOS/Linux):**\n```bash\nbrew install beads\n```\n\n**Quick Install (macOS/Linux/FreeBSD):**\n```bash\ncurl -sSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gastownhall/beads/main/scripts/install.sh | bash\n```\n\n**Windows (PowerShell):**\n```powershell\nirm https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gastownhall/beads/main/install.ps1 | iex\n```\n\n**Manual Install:**\nDownload the appropriate binary for your platform below, extract it, and place it in your PATH.\n\n\n## Changelog\n### Others\n* 10eec1f707feea8e9472ab0c0ed4ec4ed9dcb05b release(notes): align the v1.3.3 known-issue and gate notes with rc.1\n* 04a9bd02d6b8613a7dcf981487ffc3cf693dc4af release: prep v1.3.3\n\n\n\n"
